L contains no velocity of w, so the primary constraints are p_w = 0
p = dL/dv: [w3*x2 - w2*x3 + v1, -w3*x1 + w1*x3 + v2, w2*x1 - w1*x2 + v3]
d/dt p_w = [-p3*x2 + p2*x3, p3*x1 - p1*x3, -p2*x1 + p1*x2]  = -(x cross p): secondary L = x cross p = 0
{L1, L2} - L3 = 0
d/dt L - w cross L = [0, 0, 0]
x . L = 0  identically: only two of the L_i are independent
rank of d(L1, L2, L3) at x = (1, 0, 0), p = (2, 0, 0): 2
counting: N = 6, first class 3 + 2 = 5, N_phys = 6 - 5 = 1 (the radial motion)
